0033 fork/hyundai: panda safety - allow the FCA11 ESC stop-hold pair (FCA_StopReq + CF_VSM_HBACmd=1), narrowly

WHY. Route 190, 3,994 standstill frames: under our FCA11 hold the DCT clutch keeps +26 Nm (creeping); under the
driver's foot it is 0.0 Nm. CR_VSM_DecCmd pressure is injected downstream of the master-cylinder sensor, so the
car never learns it is braked. The camera's own stop-hold lane in the same frame (FCA_StopReq bit 21 +
CF_VSM_HBACmd bits 1-2) asks the ESC for ITS OWN hold. Our production FCA11 TX hook refused both bits
unconditionally, so the lane never reached the wire. We own this code; this patch allows the lane deliberately,
inside a window that can be proven from the hook alone.

ACCEPTED only when ALL hold (safety/modes/hyundai.h, HYUNDAI_FCA11_LONG_STOP_HOLD_*):
  1. exact pair: CF_VSM_HBACmd == 1 AND FCA_StopReq == 1
  2. valid variant-B actuating frame: Warn == 3, FCA_CmdAct == 1, CF_VSM_DecCmdAct == 0
  3. a real hold: CR_VSM_DecCmd >= 7 LSB (== FCA11_CRAWL_MIN_LSB, the measured clutch-open level)
  4. walking pace or less on the FASTEST wheel: max(WHL_SPD11) <= HYUNDAI_FCA11_ROLL_MIN_SPEED (160 raw = 5 km/h),
     speed seen this arm and fresh <= 100 ms (new hyundai_fca11_long_speed_max, fail-closed 0xFFFF at init).
     Fastest, not slowest: one stuck wheel must never make a moving car look stopped.
  5. the camera is not braking (hyundai_fca11_long_cam_brake keeps absolute priority)
  ...and the frame then still passes EVERY unchanged rule: 46 LSB cap, +RATE_STEP rise gate / onset rule,
  controls_allowed + heartbeat, window (seen/fresh inputs, cuts, latches, gear D, no pedal, gas hold-off),
  host-liveness watchdog, TX-stale hand-back.
REFUSED: HBA 2/3; either bit alone; either bit on a passive frame; Warn != 3; DecCmdAct set; CmdAct clear;
  DecCmd < 7; any wheel > 5 km/h; stale/unseen speed; camera braking; every pre-existing refusal.
UNCHANGED: cap, rise gate, window/clock/cut/freshness, camera hand-back and forwarding, liveness watchdog, the
  TEST-ONLY brake/rolling branches (still refuse HBA/StopReq unconditionally). No openpilot-side law change here.

Tests (safety/tests/test_hyundai.py, TestHyundaiFca11LongSafety): test_hba_stopreq_dec_cmd_act_blocked now pins the
refusal OUTSIDE the window (20 km/h, dec 1, incl. the full pair); new test_stop_hold_* cover accept at standstill,
cap/rise gate, below hold level, above walking pace (incl. single fast wheel), stale speed, HBA 2/3 + partial
pairs, frame shape (Warn/DecCmdAct/CmdAct/passive), camera braking (incl. camera's own StopReq/HBA), and every
other gate. Hyundai safety suite: 80 failed / 3071 passed before -> 80 failed / 3091 passed after; the 80 are the
identical pre-existing set (78 x test_ignore_frequency_check, F3/F5 FCA11-long). Old header + new tests: 28 fail.
Touches safety/ -> firmware bytes change -> REFLASH required.

